That was me.  You can have my code or my executable.  (Macintosh platform)
Here are my artifact changes:

+ Only lawfuls can get Excalibur from #dipping
+ Neutrals get Glossporina (a possessed long sword) by #dipping.
  (Glossporina protects from drain level, and does damage by shocking.)
  Can anyone tell me where the name comes from? (Hint: anime)
+ Stormbringer is now a long sword, and chaotics can get it by #dipping.
  "You have unleashed a water demon!"
  "The demon possesses your sword."
  (Don't cry about Mournblade or Elric.  This is just a game.)
  Stormbringer regenerates you IFF it draws life.
  There are no safe-pet or friendly warnings with Stormbringer.

+ All artifacts have fun hit messages.

So, now, with my version, all alignments have some fun artifact that protects
from drain level that they can make from #dipping a long sword, and all
the hit messages are different.  Stormbringer drains life, Excalibur "strikes,"
Glossporina "shocks."

Whaddaya think?

